    highlights: 'The Udaipur to Ahmedabad tempo traveller route connects Rajasthan\'s lake city with Gujarat\'s largest metropolis. Travel south on NH48 through the Aravalli foothills, crossing the Rajasthan-Gujarat border at Shamlaji — home to an ancient Vishnu temple worth a quick stop. The landscape transitions from rocky Aravalli terrain to the flat, fertile plains of northern Gujarat. In Ahmedabad, the UNESCO World Heritage walled old city offers Jama Masjid, the intricately carved Adalaj Stepwell, Sabarmati Ashram (Gandhi\'s home), and the modern Akshardham Temple. The Kankaria Lake evening scene and Manek Chowk\'s famous night street food market are perfect group experiences. Gujarati thali at Agashiye restaurant is a must.',
