    distance: '395 km',
    bestSeason: 'October to March (comfortable Rajasthan touring weather)',
    highlights: 'The Udaipur to Jaipur tempo traveller journey connects Rajasthan\'s two most celebrated royal cities via NH48 and NH8. The route winds through the Aravalli heartland, passing Chittorgarh — home to India\'s largest fort with its Tower of Victory, Rani Padmini\'s Palace, and stories of Rajput valor. A Chittorgarh stop adds 2-3 hours but is absolutely worth it. Further north, Bhilwara (textile city) and Ajmer (Dargah Sharif) offer break points. The drive covers diverse Rajasthani landscapes: from Udaipur\'s green lake country through rugged Mewar hills to Jaipur\'s semi-arid pink cityscape. Arriving in Jaipur, Amber Fort\'s elephant ramp, City Palace\'s royal artifacts, and Johri Bazaar\'s gemstone shops await. Dal-baati-churma at a roadside dhaba en route is an authentic experience.',
