    distance: '540 km (circuit)',
    bestSeason: 'October to February (perfect desert weather, cool evenings)',
    highlights: 'The Udaipur to Jodhpur-Jaisalmer circuit is the quintessential Rajasthan desert odyssey. From Udaipur\'s lakeside romance, drive through Ranakpur\'s Jain temple masterpiece to Jodhpur, where the mighty Mehrangarh Fort towers over the blue-washed old city. Explore the Jaswant Thada cenotaph, Umaid Bhawan Palace, and the spice-rich Sardar Market. The 285 km desert highway to Jaisalmer is a mesmerizing transition into the Thar — flat scrubland gives way to sand dunes and thorny babool trees. Jaisalmer\'s golden sandstone fort (a living fort with residents), Patwon Ki Haveli, and the Sam Sand Dunes for a camel safari and desert camp under a million stars are unforgettable. Rajasthani laal maas, ker sangri, and bajra roti fuel this royal desert adventure.',
