    distance: '285 km',
    bestSeason: 'October to February (cool desert evenings, clear skies for stargazing)',
    highlights: 'The Jodhpur to Jaisalmer tempo traveller route is a journey into the heart of the Thar Desert. Leave Mehrangarh Fort\'s blue city behind and drive west on NH-15 through increasingly barren yet beautiful desert terrain. Pokhran — where India conducted nuclear tests in 1998 — offers a fort stop and chai break. As you approach Jaisalmer, the golden sandstone Sonar Kila (Golden Fort) emerges from the desert haze like a mirage. This living fort still houses families, shops, and Jain temples within its walls. The real magic comes at Sam Sand Dunes (42 km from Jaisalmer) — camel safaris at sunset, cultural performances with Manganiyar folk musicians, and sleeping under a star-blanketed desert sky in luxury tents. Pyaaz kachori and mawa kachori in Jaisalmer are legendary.',
    stops: ['Jodhpur', 'Osiyan (ancient Jain-Hindu temples)', 'Pokhran (fort, nuclear test site)', 'Jaisalmer (Golden Fort, Patwon Haveli)', 'Sam Sand Dunes (camel safari)'],
    roadConditions: 'NH-15 (excellent flat desert highway, well-maintained, straight stretches allow smooth driving)',
